    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167-a1">

                <pb facs="0348" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg220"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 239.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Decree No</hi>. 636.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-09-25"><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 25,
                            1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President of the United States of Columbia, in execution of article 8 of law
                    53 of 1884, decrees: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. That, in accordance with
                            said law, custom-houses be established in the ports of Panama and Colon,
                            on and after the 1st of December next.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. That the import duties
                            collected therein be the same as those collected at the other ports of
                            the Republic, less 40 per cent.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 3. That the regulations common
                            to the customs service in the other ports of the Republic shall govern
                            in said ports. Consequently, that at foreign ports whence merchandise is
                            shipped thither the usual formalities as to manifests and certified
                            invoices as prescribed in articles 41, 42, 47, and 48 of the fiscal code
                            be observed.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Given at <placeName>Bogota</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1885-09-25">September 25,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>RAFAEL NUÑEZ.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Angulo</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary of War, in charge of Finance Department.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
